This remains a separately identified workaround, not a demonstrated
post-reset negotiation root-cause fix. Retry only the initial inquiry
within the existing bound; comparison reads remain fail-fast. Further
SCSI review should decide whether the controller reset path is the proper
place to recover the target agreement. It applies to vanilla v7.3-rc1.

The exact cleaned integration booted PRIMEPOWER UP/SMP from disk to
Gentoo with an ext4 root. No new post-reset DV cycle was run in this
final qualification, and the root-cause limitation above remains.
Tests used the integrated stack, not this workaround alone.

Magnus Lindholm:
  scsi: spi: retry a transient failure of the initial DV inquiry

